# Committed git hooks (opt-in: git config core.hooksPath .githooks). Un-ignored
# so the weekly current-week sync ships with the repo instead of living only on
# one machine. The script the hook calls (sync-week-marker.py) stays untracked
# like the other tooling, so the hook stands down when it is absent.
!.githooks/
!.githooks/**

# Include all files in Wk folders
!Wk1/**
!Wk2/**
!Wk3/**
!Wk4/**
!Wk5/**
!Wk6/**
!Wk7/**
!Wk9/**
!Wk10/**
!Wk11/**
!Wk12/**
!Wk13/**
!Wk14/**
!Wk15/**

# NOTE: the week list above is explicit on purpose and must be extended
# each time a new week is published. A blanket !Wk*/ would also un-ignore
# any student submission folder dropped into a week directory later in
# the term, which is exactly the data that must never be published.

# NEVER publish student submissions. Each collection folder holds homework
# uploads whose FILENAMES are student IDs and Chinese names, plus a
# teacher/Score.xls grade sheet. Publishing any of it would put 60 students'
# names, IDs and grades on a public site.
#
# This must stay AFTER every !WkN/** whitelist line above, because the last
# matching pattern wins and !Wk5/** would otherwise un-ignore the folder.
#
# The pattern is deliberately general rather than one line per folder. A second
# collection appeared in Wk5 on 7 Oct 2026 with only Wk3 blocked, so
# `git add -A` staged 61 files -- names, IDs and the grade sheet. Wk3 had been
# blocked explicitly and nothing alerted to the new folder. Matching any week
# and any suffix means the next collection folder is covered without an edit.
Wk*/1151_IM229_C_ID_*/

# Belt and braces: block any per-student upload folder wherever it appears in a
# week directory, whatever it is named.
Wk*/**/No_File_Upload.txt

# Week 9 teaching media: the 5 MB slide deck is used in class from this folder
# but is not part of the published site. The 21 MB lecture video IS published
# because the Week 9 first-task page embeds it. Un-ignored by !Wk9/**, so the
# deck must be blocked here, after that whitelist.
Wk9/Reading Skills - Skimming and Scanning - wk9.pptx

# Week 10 teaching deck: used in class from this folder, not published.
Wk10/Skimming and Scanning - wk10.pptx

# Week 10 source transcript: reference material, not part of the site.
Wk10/What_Is_Prompt_Injection.md

# Weeks 11-14 hold last year's teaching decks and LingoLeap Offline exports.
# They are source material for planning, not this year's pages, and the lesson
# exports alone are 8-11 MB each. Blocked here, after the !Wk1N/** whitelists,
# so that `git add Wk11` cannot publish them by accident.
Wk1[1-4]/*.pptx
Wk1[1-4]/*_lesson.html
Wk1[1-4]/vocabulary*.html
Wk1[1-4]/Read Aloud.html
Wk1[1-4]/dialogue.html
